From 81c2463d7ec156a8d38475d2b88753e1753021f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pseudo <cdodge@pseudoseed.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:48:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] [Spec 250][Phase: phase_8] fix: a gated architect lost
 its role caption to the gate marker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review check, and the answer was worse than 'both render'. Both DID render, on
the same line, competing for the same 230px — so a gated architect showed
'A… ● Gate: verify-approval'. That answers 'is it blocking on me' by destroying
'what agent is this', and an architect at a gate is the case a human most needs
to find.

The marker moves to the TITLE line, which has the whole row and one occupant. The
line above keeps the project label or the role caption intact. The marker does
not shrink and the title does: a row that is blocking on a person should spend
its width saying so, and titles truncate in this sidebar already.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
